  "faq1Q": "Does it work with the screen off or the app closed?",
  "faq1A": "Yes. Android itself manages the timer with an exact alarm, so it keeps running even if you close the app or turn the screen off.",
  "faq2Q": "Why does it need the Alarms & reminders permission?",
  "faq2A": "Without it, Android does not allow scheduling an alarm at an exact time and the audio could pause late. It is granted only once from the system settings.",
  "faq3Q": "What is the notification permission for?",
  "faq3A": "To show the countdown with the extend and cancel buttons. If you deny it, the timer still works, just without the notification.",
  "faq4Q": "Which apps does it work with?",
  "faq4A": "Apps that respond to the Android media controls. It has been tested with the YouTube and Twitch apps; some players may ignore them.",
  "faq5Q": "Why does the volume go down during the last minute?",
  "faq5A": "So the audio fades out gradually instead of stopping abruptly. When the time is up, Ziesta pauses the audio and leaves the volume as it was.",
  "faq6Q": "How do I extend or cancel the timer?",
  "faq6A": "From the notification, with its extend and cancel buttons, without opening the app. You can also cancel from the main screen.",
  "faq7Q": "What happens if I restart my phone?",
  "faq7A": "When the phone restarts, Android clears pending alarms, so the timer is cancelled and you would need to set it again.",
  "faq8Q": "Does Ziesta use the internet or collect data?",
  "faq8A": "No. It works offline and does not collect or send any data."
}